Relax the starlette-cramjam upper bound.

Upstream pins `starlette-cramjam>=0.4,<0.6`, but conda-forge's
starlette-cramjam feedstock has only ever built 0.7.0 -- no 0.4.x or 0.5.x
package exists in the channel, so the upstream range is unsatisfiable here.

titiler-openeo only uses `CompressionMiddleware(minimum_size=...,
exclude_mediatype=..., compression_level=...)` (titiler/openeo/main.py),
and that signature is unchanged in 0.7.0, so the cap is safe to drop.

This patch (rather than only loosening the recipe's run requirement) is
needed because `pip_check: true` validates the *installed* metadata, which
would otherwise still carry the `<0.6` cap and fail against 0.7.0.

Remove once upstream relaxes the pin:
https://github.com/sentinel-hub/titiler-openeo

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 ]
 dependencies = [
     "titiler-core>=2.0,<3.0",
-    "starlette-cramjam>=0.4,<0.6",
+    "starlette-cramjam>=0.4",
